ing, kind of similiar to Mirror, but it would be more focus on the setting and alternate gerne part, like alternate gerne that Chronicle of Darkness can be use in, and also expand on using the alternate setting for Chronicle of Darkness, like Darkness Reveal, or Darkness Destroy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not the same, but ever tried to give the Dark Eras series a look?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T23:56:16-08:00","id":1525675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525672-idea-for-chronicle-of-darkness-soucebook?p=1525673#post1525673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably not the same, but ever tried to give the Dark Eras series a look?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but while it's really great, it more alternate history than entire alternate gerne. But I would love alternate history setting for &quot;Chronicle&quot; of Darkness, and I would also love atlernate World for Chronicle of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T00:25:52-08:00","id":1525676,"title":"","content":"Maybe some sort of cyberpunk. Or dark fantasy a la Dark Souls and its children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T04:54:21-08:00","id":1525683,"title":"","content":"I think my most desired book would be a guide to cross over Chronicles that aren't contagion Chronicles. <br /> <br /> I would ideally see 4 chapters. Chapter 1 is general advice, maybe some mechanics or whatever. Chapter 2 is a focus on groups that interact more with other splats, like the eaters of the dead, but new suggestions to that book. Chapter 3 is antagonists / monsters. Chapter 4 is unusual locations that created odd alliances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T06:57:45-08:00","id":1525686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525672-idea-for-chronicle-of-darkness-soucebook?p=1525675#post1525675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but while it's really great, it more alternate history than entire alternate gerne. But I would love alternate history setting for &quot;Chronicle&quot; of Darkness, and I would also love atlernate World for Chronicle of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's because i haven't read Mirrors in quite some time, but i'd say some of the scenarios described in Dark Eras 1 &amp; 2 are much more bizarre and divergent from &quot;vanilla CotD&quot; than Darkness Revealed or Darkness Destroyed and definitely bordering on Dark Fantasy or comparable to Woundgate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T14:36:22-08:00","id":1525749,"title":"","content":"Dystopian fantasy/dystopian steampunk.<br /> <br /> High or low fantasy, but alternative history in the steam punk genre would be fun. Something where the public know about magic/vampires/werewolves, and the hunters/heroes of the world are much better equipped with knowledge to fight these groups (despite still being out matches going toe-to-toe, having numbers and largesclae organization on their side). Mages are pushed to use their powers for the political whims of human governments, and thus avoid admitting what they could actually do... Changelings and Mummys might be well known but the True Fae and Judges are far off stories told (mostly) to scare children.<br /> <br /> Each line being public would need a rethink, like removing quiesence from mage, or delerium(?) from werewolves. A steampunk setting would be fun with all of the fantasy elements this would allow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T18:14:47-08:00","id":1525764,"title":"","content":"An actual Dark-Ages source book for Requiem/Forsaken/MtA: and a Victorian-Age/Wild West source-book (probably mentioned in <i>Dark Eras</i>); and no, source-books about the future; WoD belongs in the past; it just doesn't seem to fit in science-fiction. But that's just my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-igua